I think I always want shorter timers.

00:28:49.940 --> 00:28:52.500
It was probably Anticipation.

00:28:53.500 --> 00:28:54.700
Okay, maybe it was that.

00:28:54.780 --> 00:28:55.940
I thought it was... Oh, you know what?

00:28:56.000 --> 00:28:57.120
No, it was Jeopardy, right?

00:28:57.420 --> 00:28:58.300
Jeopardy, or...

00:28:58.300 --> 00:28:59.280
No, not Family Feud.

00:28:59.400 --> 00:29:00.560
We didn't even play that. Wheel of Fortune?

00:29:00.820 --> 00:29:03.620
I don't even know. Something gave you, I think it was Jeopardy,

00:29:03.700 --> 00:29:06.480
they gave you, like, a... They gave you not enough time or something like that.

00:29:06.600 --> 00:29:08.360
I wanted more time. But this happens all the time.

00:29:08.560 --> 00:29:10.660
I even choose time, you know, I'm fluctuating.

00:29:11.020 --> 00:29:14.640
Yeah. No, I mean, I do like that idea, though,

00:29:14.840 --> 00:29:18.940
of at least in a one-on-one, like, person versus person,

00:29:19.080 --> 00:29:20.160
that is interesting to me.

00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:21.560
I don't really know how useful it would come

00:29:22.160 --> 00:29:23.060
against a computer,

00:29:23.060 --> 00:29:25.180
which is making these decisions much faster,

00:29:25.320 --> 00:29:28.120
but for sure, I like that.

00:30:08.140 --> 00:30:14.920
And did you guys notice that when you start up this game with awful music,

